A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||cheap alternative to turbos!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-27-2000||04:48 PM||||a friend and I were messing around with his nissan maxima (its fiero related, wait!) with a mildly modded 3.0 v6, about 190 hp, auto. from a rolling start I usually smack him down. well, we were in my garage, and decided to f*** with his car. we took 3 leaf blowers, a bunch of pvc attachments, some flexible tubing, and a big 3" diameter valve that I made (allows it to breathe while the leaf blowers are not on, stops pushed air from going back out the airtube) well, we piled all these in the back seat of his car, plugged them in (he has a power inverter, that how we power the computer and the monitor and camera that all my moving car videos are filmed from) and we test fired it to see how much air is moved by 3 leaf blowers going from 3- 4" inlets to 3 2.5" exits, to 3" tubing, and it blew a godawful amount of air. we then jumpstarted the car (killed the battery) my brother got in the back seat, and we all went out for a drive. we are side by side going about thirty, i rev, he gets on it and I am pulling, then I hear his engine make a godawful howl and he pulls on me, gets into his rev range, and toasted me (not realy, but he pulled ahead). after a few minutes his car died and the check engine light came on. now it was not a dramatic difference, but i think it would be cool to put that on a dyno and see what happens? oh yeah, after we got back, it became apparent that when we shut off the blowers, it sucked air out of the engine, as there was a bunch of oil in the tubes. all in all it was pretty cool. I want a real turbo, or a bunch of them!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-27-2000||06:04 PM||||Last year I found a vent fan that moves 1280 CFM..<P>it's $60 at Home Hardware.. 120v AC, but an inverter can be used<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-27-2000||09:41 PM||||Jeesh, I thought everyone had heard of deckercharging! <P>I know of someone who put a squirrel cage fan on their Toyota. They ran the fan off of the alternator pulley (it had a spare pulley that used to be for the A/C. Then ducted the fan into the intake. It revved the snot out of the motor and blew apart the fan!||||reg||1
